  "summary": "Hagia Sophia, the Church of the Holy Wisdom, was built at Constantinople for Emperor Justinian between 532 and 537, under a central dome about 31 m across. It became a mosque after the Ottoman conquest of 1453, a museum in 1934, and a mosque again in 2020.",
